welcome to the David Pakman show I am  fairing cousin sitting in for David  Pakman today if you've been paying  attention to Donald Trump's Twitter feed  as I know most of us like to do from  time to time you kind of get the feeling  that this man never really knows exactly  what he wants to say about anything but  one thing we can always count on is the  fact that eventually every day or so  he's gonna start talking about the  alleged witch-hunt being launched by  robert muller and those 13 angry  democrats on the special prosecutors  team but what we really need to  understand here though is that donald  trump is repeating the exact same failed  strategy that richard nixon used to  avoid the watergate scandal in the  months leading up to the firing of  special prosecutor Archibald Cox back in  the Watergate investigation when all  that was at its peak the Nixon team  Nixon and his lawyers came up with a new  strategy they were tired of trying to  tell the public he had done nothing  wrong he'd done nothing wrong so what  they did was they switched and they  began to launch attacks against  Archibald Cox they called it a witch  hunt I'm sure we've all seen the images  of those old newspaper clippings that  say Nixon sees witch-hunt an  investigation and they called him a  partisan hack saying that this was  launched for political purposes they  know there's nothing there  but they're going to do it anyway this  was a losing strategy for Nixon nobody  in the public actually bought into this  but nonetheless they use this very  flimsy pretext as their justification to  eventually fire the special prosecutor  that's you know the Saturday night  massacre everybody for the last year  here in the United States has been  waiting to see if Donald Trump is going  to launch his own Saturday night  Massacre and fire Robert Muller shut  down the special prosecutor's office but  again we go back to Nixon because what  Nixon had to do then after he fired Cox  he had to appoint another special  prosecutor you see they couldn't just  exactly end the investigation they had  already been gathering evidence they  were already talking to people they had  pretty much built their case at that  point yet it wasn't quite finished so  they hire the new special prosecutor who  after seeing what happened to the last  one realized you know what I've got to  do this pretty quickly and that is  exactly what happened after the special  prosecutor finished got a couple of uh  you know pleas from some of the people  involved in Watergate they then went and  presented what has been described as a  mountain of evidence as the basis for  impeachment against Richard Nixon and as  we all know Richard Nixon never got to  the point of impeachment because he  resigned because he understood he didn't  have the votes to save himself from that  there's not too much different from what  Donald Trump is doing right now compared  to what Nixon did back then but right  now we're still at kind of the planning  phase if you recall a few months ago  Rudy Giuliani made it very clear that  their new legal strategy was going to be  to try to discredit Muller and his team  that way whenever evidence eventually  came out you know whether it was against  the Trump associate or against Trump  himself the hardcore truckers in this  country wouldn't believe that it was  real if they spent enough time just  crediting this guy telling everyone he's  a partisan hack even though he's a  registered Republican they could  absolutely be certain that the public  would never support any kind of removal  of Donald Trump from the Oval Office  again unfortunately doesn't appear to be  working right now polls show that at  least half of this country is all on  board with impeachment so Trump if he's  going to continue following in the  footsteps of Richard Nixon his next move  could be to fire Robert Muller and a lot  of people are very frightened by that  prospect you know if he fires Muller  we 